A website remembers whether the user chose dark mode.
```javascript
const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
if (savedTheme === 'dark') {
  document.body.classList.add('dark');
}
document.getElementById('dark').addEventListener('click', () => {
  document.body.classList.add('dark');
  localStorage.setItem('theme', 'dark');
});
```
(a) A user visits the site for the first time. What does localStorage.getItem('theme') return, and is the page shown in dark mode?
(b) The user clicks the button, closes the browser, and comes back the next day. Is the page in dark mode? Explain why.
(c) The developer deletes the localStorage.setItem line. What happens now when the user clicks the button and then reloads the page?

A button shows a message when it is clicked.
```html
<button id="greet">Say hello</button>
<p id="message"></p>
```
```javascript
const button = document.getElementById('greet');
const message = document.getElementById('message');
function showMessage() {
  message.textContent = 'Hello!';
}
button.addEventListener('click', showMessage);
```
(a) What does the user see when the page first loads, and what happens when they click the button?
(b) The developer changes the last line to `button.addEventListener('click', showMessage());`. What happens now, and why?
(c) The developer changes `'click'` to `'mouseover'`. When does the message appear now?

A sign-up form shows a welcome message.
```html
<form id="signup">
  <input id="name" type="text">
  <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
</form>
<p id="output"></p>
```
```javascript
const form = document.getElementById('signup');
form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
  event.preventDefault();
  const name = document.getElementById('name').value;
  document.getElementById('output').textContent = 'Welcome, ' + name;
});
```
(a) The user types Sam into the box and clicks Sign up. What is shown on the page? Explain where the name comes from.
(b) The developer deletes the `event.preventDefault();` line. What happens now when the form is submitted?
(c) The developer wants to stop the form from being submitted when the name box is empty, without writing any JavaScript. What should they add to the HTML, and what happens if the user then clicks Sign up with the box empty?

