```javascript
function counter() {
  let count = 0;
  return () => ++count;
}
const next = counter();
console.log(next(), next(), next());
```
(a) What is printed, and why?
(b) Why can the returned function still read `count` after `counter` has finished running?
(c) What is a closure, in one sentence?

